    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-the-worker-can-loop-from-21": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-the-worker-can-loop-from-21",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The worker can loop from validation back into planning while evidence is getting\nsharper and budget remains. New facts and blockers are evidence attached to the\nworker state; workers do not coordinate through direct worker-to-worker chat."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-write-set-widening-67": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-write-set-widening-67",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Write-Set Widening"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-a-claim-begins-with-68": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-a-claim-begins-with-68",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A claim begins with the target source as its only approved category. When that\nscope cannot express the canonical fix, the worker follows the necessity ladder:\nin-slice typing, config metadata, the owning header, then foreign source. Each\nrequest names the paths and category, the mismatched declaration or symbol, the\nexpected owner, measured objdiff evidence, and why every lower rung failed."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-widening-decisions-use-69": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-widening-decisions-use-69",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The widening request travels in the checkpoint handoff note. The runner checks\nthat its paths share one category and that the evidence covers the lower rungs,\nthen approves, denies, defers, or routes the request. Approval expands the live\nclaim and returns continuation instructions; every other decision returns a\nreason so the worker can preserve the best lower-rung result without adding a\nlocal alias, prototype, or include shim."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-a-recycled-target-reset-70": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-a-recycled-target-reset-70",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A recycled or re-picked-up target resets to its target-source write set. The new\nworker re-earns every wider category from fresh evidence; prior requests and\ndecisions remain telemetry, not authorization."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-capabilities-22": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-capabilities-22",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Capabilities"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-capabilities-are-tactics-23": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-capabilities-are-tactics-23",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Capabilities are tactics available to a worker. They are not separate worker\ntypes. A single worker can combine context packaging, type and symbol\nresolution, duplicate adaptation, focused source editing, fact research,\nisolated check loops, review cleanup, experimental search, and permuter handoff\nwhen the target packet and evidence justify them."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-experimental-search-is-o-24": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-experimental-search-is-o-24",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Experimental search is opt-in. It is useful when a worker can define a bounded,\nmeasurable matrix of source-shape variants. It should produce shards, negative\nresults, and learned patterns rather than unreviewable random mutations."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-the-full-capability-tabl-25": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-the-full-capability-tabl-25",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The full capability table and guardrails live in\n"
        },
        {
          "insert": "worker capabilities",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "10-system-design/50-workflows/20-run/40-workers/20-capabilities",
              "label": "worker capabilities"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-runner-validation-26": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-runner-validation-26",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Runner Validation"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-runner-validation-is-the-27": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-runner-validation-is-the-27",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Runner validation is the source of truth for progress. The runner captures a\npre-worker baseline, diffs the approved write set after each attempt, runs local\nvalidation over the touched set and its immediate compile blast, records a\ncheckpoint, and decides whether that checkpoint is selectable."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-the-pre-worker-object-bu-28": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-the-pre-worker-object-bu-28",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The pre-worker object build and later validation builds are narrow worker-local\ncommands, not full game report rebuilds. A target-source edit rebuilds and\ndiffs its unit; foreign-source edits add their units, owning-header edits add the\nowner and direct includers, and config-metadata edits add the affected address-\nrange units and section measures. Compile-heavy "
        },
        {
          "insert": "ninja",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " calls acquire\nan epoch-scoped worker Ninja slot before running in the worker worktree. Worker\nPi tools that invoke MWCC or objdiff use the toolpack's own per-tool slot pools,\nso a worker may keep its conversation alive while waiting for a local build or\ncheckdiff/permuter slot."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-a-checkpoint-records-29": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-a-checkpoint-records-29",
