    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-only-checkpoints-that-pa-35": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-only-checkpoints-that-pa-35",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Only checkpoints that pass hard gates and improve over the worker state's\nbaseline are selectable. Best-checkpoint selection is deterministic: exact match\nwins, then highest target score, then earliest validation time. Failed or\nneutral checkpoints remain useful evidence, but they are not integration\ncandidates."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-a-checkpoint-can-measure-36": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-a-checkpoint-can-measure-36",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A checkpoint can measure an exact target score while still failing hard gates\nsuch as QA lint, post-return checks, or local validation. That checkpoint is\nnot selectable and does not close the worker as exact. It is treated as\nhigh-value repair evidence and receives the bounded failed-gate exact repair\nbudget described below."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-runner-owned-validation-37": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-runner-owned-validation-37",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Runner-owned validation also runs the worker-side QA lint (the QA ship gate's\nL1 layer; see "
        },
        {
          "insert": "score and PR handoff",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "10-system-design/50-workflows/30-pr/10-score-gate-and-handoff",
              "label": "score and PR handoff"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": "). The runner\ndiffs the attempt's touched files against the pre-worker source snapshot and\nruns the deterministic maintainer-rejection scan over that diff. Findings\nbecome repair feedback. A score-improving attempt that re-adds or leaves a QA\nfinding is rejected because the finding may be what inflated the score. Any\nout-of-write-set path is also categorized, recorded in attempt telemetry, and\nreturned as a repair reason; the worker must justify a widening request or\nrevert it before the attempt can bank."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-scanner-infrastructure-e-38": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-scanner-infrastructure-e-38",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Scanner infrastructure errors are recorded as blind spots rather than mass\nworker failures. The PR handoff gate remains stricter and fails closed."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-global-score-integration-39": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-global-score-integration-39",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A selectable checkpoint that passes its scoped checks banks as tentative. With\nmerge-on-finish enabled it is applied serially to the cycle ancestry when the\nworker closes; otherwise it follows the queued integration path. The epoch\nboundary global check confirms clean tentative items. A regression is attributed\nto the tentative window, the guilty change is reverted and marked regressed, and\nthe clean remainder becomes confirmed."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-worker-state-outcomes-40": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-worker-state-outcomes-40",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Worker State Outcomes"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-worker-state-lifecycle-s-41": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-worker-state-lifecycle-s-41",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Worker state lifecycle status describes why execution ended:"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-exact-runner-valida-42": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-exact-runner-valida-42",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Exact",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": runner validation selected an exact checkpoint."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-timeout-the-runner-43": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-timeout-the-runner-43",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Timeout",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": the runner-controlled timeout ended the attempt; the best prior"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-selectable-checkpoint-is-44": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-selectable-checkpoint-is-44",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "  selectable checkpoint is preserved, or baseline is selected when none\n  improved."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-error-a-provider-i-45": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-error-a-provider-i-45",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Error",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": a provider, infrastructure, tool, build, parse, or agent session failure"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-blocked-trustworthy-eval-46": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-blocked-trustworthy-eval-46",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "  blocked trustworthy evaluation. Prior selectable checkpoints remain usable."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-cancelled-an-operat-47": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-cancelled-an-operat-47",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Cancelled",
          "attributes": {
            "bold": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ": an operator or process-control path stopped the worker before"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-normal-lifecycle-close-48": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-normal-lifecycle-close-48",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "  normal lifecycle close."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-improvement-neutrality-49": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-improvement-neutrality-49",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Improvement, neutrality, regression, and exactness are validation/verdict facts,\nnot worker-authored stop claims. The dashboard and knowledge curator read\nworker states and checkpoints rather than asking the worker to classify its own\ndurable outcome."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-continuation-policy-50": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-continuation-policy-50",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Continuation Policy"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-a-worker-continues-only-51": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-a-worker-continues-only-51",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A worker continues only while runner-owned evidence says more attempts are\nworth spending:"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-an-accepted-exact-checkp-52": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-an-accepted-exact-checkp-52",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "An accepted exact checkpoint stops immediately."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-a-cold-worker-with-no-se-53": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-a-cold-worker-with-no-se-53",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A cold worker with no selectable improvement and no failed-gate exact"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-checkpoint-stops-after-t-54": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-checkpoint-stops-after-t-54",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "  checkpoint stops after the fifth human attempt."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-the-first-selectable-non-55": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-the-first-selectable-non-55",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The first selectable non-exact improvement is saved immediately. The worker"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-can-spend-up-to-three-fo-56": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-can-spend-up-to-three-fo-56",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "  can spend up to three follow-up checkpoints looking for a new best or exact."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-a-higher-selectable-best-57": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-a-higher-selectable-best-57",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "A higher selectable best resets the three-follow-up budget."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-if-three-follow-up-check-58": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-if-three-follow-up-check-58",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "If three follow-up checkpoints after the latest best do not produce a higher"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-selectable-best-or-exact-59": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-selectable-best-or-exact-59",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "  selectable best or exact, the worker stops and the saved best checkpoint is\n  preserved."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-an-exact-score-that-fail-60": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-an-exact-score-that-fail-60",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "An exact score that fails hard gates starts a failed-gate exact repair lane."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-the-runner-can-spend-up-61": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-the-runner-can-spend-up-61",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "  The runner can spend up to three follow-up checkpoints repairing the gates,\n  even when the cold budget would otherwise stop the worker."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-if-the-failed-gate-exact-62": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-if-the-failed-gate-exact-62",
      "type": "list-item",
      "props": {
        "ordered": false
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "If the failed-gate exact repair lane does not produce an accepted exact or a"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-selectable-best-within-i-63": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-selectable-best-within-i-63",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "  selectable best within its follow-up budget, the worker stops."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-when-the-runner-rejects-64": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-when-the-runner-rejects-64",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "When the runner rejects a checkpoint or accepts a non-exact checkpoint for\ncontinued work, the same worker conversation receives repair or continuation\nfeedback. That feedback names the validation failure, QA finding, non-exact\nscore, widening decision, categorized out-of-write-set paths, and continuation\nreason so the worker can refine without losing context."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "b-40-worker-lifecycle-the-claim-deadline-dry-65": {
      "id": "b-40-worker-lifecycle-the-claim-deadline-dry-65",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The claim deadline, dry-run mode, provider failures, and missing repair reasons\nstill stop continuation. At timeout, the runner chooses the best validated state\nrather than trusting the worker's self-assessment."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    }
  }
}
